mjO=am2(mjN),mj2=Ce(mj1,'\nPlaces probes on the bindings at the given paths to observe their runtime values.\nWhen a probe is active, the agent view shows evaluated values at line ends (e.g., `expr  #\xe2\x80\xba \xe2\x89\xa1 value #`).\nThis is a powerful debugging and verification tool \xe2\x80\x94 use it to check whether code behaves as expected.\nPlacing a probe opens its entry, so the results show.\nValues come from the evaluator; the next context refresh waits for evaluation to finish, so probe values are normally present immediately. A `\xe2\x88\x85` means the probed expression was never reached during evaluation (e.g. a branch not taken or a function never called) \xe2\x80\x94 that itself is useful evidence.\n\nParameters:\npaths: list(string) \xe2\x80\x94 paths to the bindings to probe\n\nExample:\nGiven the program:\n```\nlet double(x) = x * 2 in\nlet result = double(5) in\nresult\n```\nCalling place_probe(paths=["result"]) shows:\n```\n#\xe2\x80\xba program map \xc2\xb7 no errors #\n'+aXF+"\nlet double(x) = \xe2\x8b\xaf in  #\xe2\x80\xba 1 use #\nlet result = \xe2\x8b\xaf in  #\xe2\x80\xba open below \xc2\xb7 1 use #\nresult  #\xe2\x80\xba \xe2\x87\x92 10 #\n\n#\xe2\x80\xba open entries, in full #\n#\xe2\x80\xba open: result #\nlet result = \xe2\x9f\xa6double(5)\xe2\x9f\xa7 in  #\xe2\x80\xba \xe2\x89\xa1 10 #\n```\nThe \xe2\x89\xa1 10 shows that `result`'s probed expression, in \xe2\x9f\xa6 \xe2\x9f\xa7, evaluates to 10.\n\n"+I_+caX,[0,[0,mj0,_v(mjZ)],0],mjY),mj7=Ce(mj6,'\nRemoves probes from the bindings at the given paths.\nUse this to clean up probes after verifying code behavior.\n\nParameters:\npaths: list(string) \xe2\x80\x94 paths to the bindings to remove probes from\n\nExample:\nCalling remove_probe(paths=["result"]) removes the probe from "result",\nand the view no longer shows evaluated values for that binding.\n\n'+I_+caX,[0,[0,mj5,_v(mj4)],0],mj3);function
